<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17126" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ex-pugnābĭlis</span></b> ,
		e, adj.
		expugno, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>that may be taken</i>, <i>carried</i>, or <i>reduced by assault;
			expugnable</i> (very rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">urbs terra marique expugnabilis est,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					33, 17, 8</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ne magnis quidem exercitibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. H.
					3, 78</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">situ non expugnabile robur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 6, 103</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fluvius,</span>”
				i. e. <i>exhaustible</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 4, 836</span></i>
			.</div>
